clueweb09-en0007-85-36519.0 Dutchess County Tourism Search Events Calendar: Search Events by Location: All Amenia Annandale-on-Hudson Beacon Beekman Clinton Corners Dover Plains Fishkill Germantown Hopewell Junction Hyde Park LaGrange Lagrangeville Millbrook Millerton Pawling Pine Plains Pleasant Valley Poughkeepsie Poughquag Red Hook Rhinebeck Staatsburg Stanford Stormville Tivoli Wappingers Falls Wassaic Wingdale RESOURCES Properties Property News Maps & Directions Photo Gallery Press Room Contact Us About Us Home Meeting and Event Planning Professionals Property News Dutchess Manor Completes Renovations If you haven't been to Dutchess Manor lately, you are in for a pleasant surprise. The Coris family spent the winter months completely renovating and updating the historically acclaimed mansion that has been in their family since 1947. They enclosed part of an outdoor deck so as to enlarge the indoor cocktail space. The décor was updated with care, transforming the banquet room colors to soft creams and buttery yellows. The gleaming chandeliers and mirrors ensure the feeling of
clueweb09-en0007-85-36519.125 Dutchess County Tourism décor was updated with care, transforming the banquet room colors to soft creams and buttery yellows. The gleaming chandeliers and mirrors ensure the feeling of refinement has not changed! Although the interior has been modified, one thing that has not been altered is the stunning view of the Hudson River and its western shore. Set far above the banks of the Hudson River, Dutchess Manor provides a unique setting for memorable events. Built during the 1860's, the red stone exterior and Victorian architecture convey a feeling of elegance from a bygone era. Dutchess Manor's scrumptious cuisine matches the sophisticated ambiance. From April through early November, the outdoor terraces, gazebo and lawn areas are accessible, giving you the chance to stroll along and enjoy the scenic river vistas. Call 845/831-3650 and ask for one of the brothers, Harry or Dean Coris, whose obvious pride in their vocation means excellence in hospitality
clueweb09-en0007-85-36519.250 Dutchess County Tourism river vistas. Call 845/831-3650 and ask for one of the brothers, Harry or Dean Coris, whose obvious pride in their vocation means excellence in hospitality for their customers. Dutchess Manor is located on Route 9D in Beacon just minutes from Interstate Route 84. http://www.dutchessmanor.com Best Western Inn Adds Zing with New Indian Restaurant The Best Western Inn has spiced things up with their new Indian Restaurant, Spice Aroma! Check out the all you can eat lunch buffet, served Monday through Friday from 11:30am to 2:30 pm. For only $8.95, you can check out all kind of delicious Indian treats. Specialties include Chicken Tikka Masala, baked in a clay oven; Khorna Kashmiri (lamb or goat!) and plenty of vegetarian dishes. Some of these mouth-watering meals include Vegetable Jalfrezi (cooked with garlic and ginger), and Saag Paneer - homemade cottage cheese with spinach and spices! Add a little zing to your life
clueweb09-en0007-85-36519.375 Dutchess County Tourism Vegetable Jalfrezi (cooked with garlic and ginger), and Saag Paneer - homemade cottage cheese with spinach and spices! Add a little zing to your life with a little something new. They also serve a weekend buffet served from noon to 3pm for $10.95. They offer flavorful lunch boxes, available to take out for those on the go. The Best Western is located at 2170 South Rd. Call 845/462-4600 for information. www.bestwestern.com/innconfctrpoughkeepsie . For A Memorable Meeting, Conferen e Or Event Experience, Think Dutchess! Learn more about our properties About DCT | Advertise with Us | Contact Us | Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Home (C) 2006 Dutchess County Tourism. All rights reserved. Dutchess County Tourism, 3 Neptune Rd. Suite Q-17, Poughkeepsie NY 12601 Tel: 845/463-4000 or 800/445-3131 The programs provided by this agency are partially funded by monies received from the County of Dutchess.
